      "id": 2,
      "claim": "All known salmon species conduct spawning (egg deposition and fertilisation) exclusively in freshwater habitats, never in saltwater.",
      "evidence": "Empirical studies of Atlantic salmon (Salmo salar) and Pacific salmon (Oncorhynchus spp.) show fertilisation occurs on riverbeds or lake substrates; no marine spawning has been documented.",
